 "intro": "Syracuse, Sicily, 214-212 BC. The great Greek city has gone over to Carthage. You are Marcus Claudius Marcellus, attacking by land and sea, against defences designed by the mathematician Archimedes.",
 "debrief": "In the accounts of Polybius, Livy and Plutarch, Archimedes’s catapults and cranes, which lifted ships from the water and dropped them, defeated the first Roman assault, and Marcellus turned to a blockade. In 212 BC, during a festival of Artemis, Romans climbed a low stretch of wall at night and took the Epipolae. A Carthaginian relief army was destroyed by plague in the marshes. The inner city fell when a Spanish officer opened a gate. Archimedes was killed by a soldier, against Marcellus’s orders. The other choices are what-ifs.",
